TTYCHATTER.PYTHON(1)        User Commands        TTYCHATTER.PYTHON(1)

NAME
    ttychatter.python - Bash terminal client with Python 3 helper routines

SYNOPSIS
    ttychatter.python [session]
    ttychatter.python --resume <session|session.log|/path/session.log>
    ttychatter.python --models
    ttychatter.python --update-models
    ttychatter.python --test-model <model_id>
    ttychatter.python --select-model
    ttychatter.python --doctor
    ttychatter.python --demo
    ttychatter.python --version
    ttychatter.python --loopback
    ttychatter.python --loopback-file <path>
    ttychatter.python --help

DESCRIPTION
    ttychatter.python is the full line-oriented terminal client for
    ttychatter. Bash orchestrates the user workflow and Python 3 helper snippets
    handle JSON, URL/path handling, attachment extraction, and log parsing.

API KEYS
    API keys may be loaded from:
        OPENROUTER_API_KEY
        TTYCHATTER_API_KEY
        OPENROUTER_API_KEY or API_KEY in config
        API_KEY_GPG_FILE via gpg decryption

    The default encrypted key file is:
        ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/api-key.gpg

    GPG support is optional and uses the user's external gpg command.

RUNTIME COMMAND MODE
    During interactive chat, inputs beginning with ':' are local commands rather
    than messages to OpenRouter. Examples:
        :help
        :models
        :select-model
        :test-model openrouter/auto
        :set CONTEXT_TURNS 20
        :memory
        :attach ./notes.txt
        :credits
        :quit

LOOPBACK OUTPUT
    ttychatter.python --loopback
        Runs the interactive chat normally, but sends prompts, status text,
        separators, and runtime-command output to stderr while clean AI
        responses are written to stdout. This allows the user to pipe AI
        responses into another program without mixing user-interface text into
        the pipe.

    ttychatter.python --loopback-file <path>
        Appends each AI response to the named file while preserving the normal
        interactive display.

DEMO MODE
    --demo provides local model rows and local AI responses. It is useful for
    testing sessions, command mode, and attachment extraction without making
    OpenRouter chat requests.

VERSION
    ttychatter.python version 3.7
